Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: jank
Upstream-Contact: Jeaye Wilkerson <jeaye@jank-lang.org>
Source: https://github.com/jank-lang/jank
Comment:
 The orig tarball is made by tools/make-orig in the packaging repository: jank at
 one commit with its git submodules (immer's nested, unused submodules excluded),
 plus zstd and libdwarf-lite, which cpptrace would otherwise download at configure
 time. compiler+runtime/third-party/debian-vendor/SOURCES lists the URL and commit
 or SHA-256 of every component.
 .
 libdwarf-lite (LGPL-2.1) and zstd (used under BSD-3-Clause) are linked statically
 into /usr/bin/jank. The corresponding source is this source package, distributed
 alongside the binary package.
 .
 Where a component's licence file names no copyright holder, the stanza names the
 component's contributors.

